# Product boundaries

- Do not treat the initial-infrastructure specification as proof of implemented behavior; verify code before describing it as current state.
- Do not add a production review rule beyond `template-noop` during initial infrastructure work; use the test-only fixture rule for finding behavior.
- Do not turn review findings into build failures or automatically refactor reviewed code.
- Do not make architecture, size, complexity, coupling, or context-dependent performance advice a build-breaking analyzer diagnostic. Reserve analyzer errors for concrete technical defects.
- Do not add dynamic rule loading, a separate daemon, or a dependency from Core to CLI or MCP. Follow the contracts in `tasks/initial-infrastructure/epics/`.
- Do not write Serilog events to stdout or stderr, or resolve the log directory from the working directory or analyzed project's paths. Follow the executable-relative logging contract in [Epic 1](../../tasks/initial-infrastructure/epics/01-Eingaben-und-Host.md#logging).
